<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Buyid dynasty</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Buyids, Buyid</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Buyid dynasty was a Shia Iranian dynasty from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/daylam">Daylam</a> that controlled much of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iraq">Iraq</a> in the tenth and eleventh centuries. After taking <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baghdad">Baghdad</a> in 945, the Buyids ruled while keeping the Abbasid <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate">caliphs</a> as figureheads. They were displaced by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seljuk-empire">Seljuk Turks</a>, whose leader <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tughril">Tughril Beg</a> entered Baghdad in 1055, a key step in the rise of the Seljuk Empire.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/buyid-dynasty.jpg" alt="Buyid dynasty" width="320" height="204" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: ro4444 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Buyids_970.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
